 The Company’s manpower outsourcing business provides workforce sourcing and deployment services, including casual labor sourced principally through the YY App.","section":"BUSINESS OVERVIEW","block":13,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001185185-26-004297","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-09-25","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001985337","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1985337/000118518526004297/yyforceex99-2.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/e8a2dc97dd8a0ddfefc4f73ee7514046e6d0fa33ca985c39bf1a858e6068ec80.bin","sha256":"e8a2dc97dd8a0ddfefc4f73ee7514046e6d0fa33ca985c39bf1a858e6068ec80"}},{"id":"31425e758252f6bfa921fac32f8d1494c83cea37a4048f216bf3e204e42fd0d4","quote":"The Company operates across multiple markets. As disclosed in the Company’s unaudited condensed consolidated financial statements, our business operations include Singapore, Malaysia, Hong Kong, Thailand, Vietnam, the Netherlands and the United Arab Emirates, with the majority of its revenue generated from Singapore, Malaysia and Hong Kong.","context":"For the six months ended June 30, 2026, these two principal businesses represented approximately 96.8% of the Company’s consolidated revenue, compared with approximately 93.3% for the corresponding period in 2025.","section":"BUSINESS OVERVIEW","block":14,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001185185-26-004297","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-09-25","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001985337","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1985337/000118518526004297/yyforceex99-2.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/e8a2dc97dd8a0ddfefc4f73ee7514046e6d0fa33ca985c39bf1a858e6068ec80.bin","sha256":"e8a2dc97dd8a0ddfefc4f73ee7514046e6d0fa33ca985c39bf1a858e6068ec80"}},{"id":"c34658a7915043d1fa85f854d1f27fa2749b60204dfcc171ad4c769537e60b78","quote":"Strategic Direction - YYForce 2030 Future Workforce Vision","context":"The Company operates across multiple markets. As disclosed in the Company’s unaudited condensed consolidated financial statements, our business operations include Singapore, Malaysia, Hong Kong, Thailand, Vietnam, the Netherlands and the United Arab Emirates, with the majority of its revenue generated from Singapore, Malaysia and Hong Kong.","section":"BUSINESS OVERVIEW","block":15,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001185185-26-004297","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-09-25","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001985337","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1985337/000118518526004297/yyforceex99-2.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/e8a2dc97dd8a0ddfefc4f73ee7514046e6d0fa33ca985c39bf1a858e6068ec80.bin","sha256":"e8a2dc97dd8a0ddfefc4f73ee7514046e6d0fa33ca985c39bf1a858e6068ec80"}},{"id":"aab8127ee58bf2bbbfd6c095fcae3d29908fc5b5a42c480145b501438f5aa1bf","quote":"As the Company expands its existing businesses, the Company is also pursuing a longer-term strategy intended to evolve YYForce from a predominantly labor-intensive workforce outsourcing and facility services provider toward a broader future workforce solutions provider.","context":"Strategic Direction - YYForce 2030 Future Workforce Vision","section":"BUSINESS OVERVIEW","block":16,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001185185-26-004297","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-09-25","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001985337","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1985337/000118518526004297/yyforceex99-2.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/e8a2dc97dd8a0ddfefc4f73ee7514046e6d0fa33ca985c39bf1a858e6068ec80.bin","sha256":"e8a2dc97dd8a0ddfefc4f73ee7514046e6d0fa33ca985c39bf1a858e6068ec80"}},{"id":"e973ce1117989767ba540f2860580ef73941393b58a1eed2191323a48ce75a98","quote":"The Company’s long-term strategic direction is based on its view that human workers, digital workforce platforms, artificial intelligence, smart facility-management technologies, automation and robotics may increasingly operate together within workforce-intensive industries.","context":"As the Company expands its existing businesses, the Company is also pursuing a longer-term strategy intended to evolve YYForce from a predominantly labor-intensive workforce outsourcing and facility services provider toward a broader future workforce solutions provider.","section":"BUSINESS OVERVIEW","block":17,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001185185-26-004297","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-09-25","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001985337","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1985337/000118518526004297/yyforceex99-2.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/e8a2dc97dd8a0ddfefc4f73ee7514046e6d0fa33ca985c39bf1a858e6068ec80.bin","sha256":"e8a2dc97dd8a0ddfefc4f73ee7514046e6d0fa33ca985c39bf1a858e6068ec80"}},{"id":"9d53b002adfd743e557fd33fcb8c7c3a13313313a81b28e48b50b839a35c37c5","quote":"Human Workforce. The Company’s existing manpower outsourcing operations provide workforce sourcing, deployment and workforce-management capabilities across multiple markets.","context":"The Company’s long-term strategic direction is based on its view that human workers, digital workforce platforms, artificial intelligence, smart facility-management technologies, automation and robotics may increasingly operate together within workforce-intensive industries.","section":"BUSINESS OVERVIEW","block":18,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001185185-26-004297","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-09-25","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001985337","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1985337/000118518526004297/yyforceex99-2.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/e8a2dc97dd8a0dd