y incorporated technology-enabled workforce management and expanded into Smart IFM. The Group is currently focused on developing its Smart IFM capabilities, while exploring the use of automation and robotics to enhance operational efficiency and service delivery. Over time, the Group aims to integrate workforce management, IFM, technology, automation and robotics into a broader platform of integrated future workforce solutions.","context":"Workforce Outsourcing -> Technology-Enabled Workforce Management -> Smart IFM -> Automation & Robotics -> Integrated Future Workforce Solutions","section":"BUSINESS OVERVIEW","block":33,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001185185-26-004297","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-09-25","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001985337","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1985337/000118518526004297/yyforceex99-2.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/e8a2dc97dd8a0ddfefc4f73ee7514046e6d0fa33ca985c39bf1a858e6068ec80.bin","sha256":"e8a2dc97dd8a0ddfefc4f73ee7514046e6d0fa33ca985c39bf1a858e6068ec80"}}],"omittedEvidenceCount":0},"operatingKpis":{"status":"evidence_available","evidence":[{"id":"c09d90c709617ce3e0e10397a2c48b80d2d1c3803d8b8ce579c5977810d55ffb","quote":"For the six months ended June 30, 2026, the Company’s capital expenditures related principally to cleaning machinery, computer equipment and other operational tools supporting the expansion of its IFM and manpower outsourcing businesses. Purchases of property and equipment and intangible assets totalled $380,527 during the period. These investments supported productivity, digitalization and operating capacity across the Company’s service divisions.","context":"Capital Expenditures","section":"RESULTS OF OPERATIONS","block":124,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001185185-26-004297","form":"6-K","filedAt"